<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Prediction Market Lab — research report</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --ink: #16181d;
    --muted: #6b7280;
    --faint: #e6e7ea;
    --band: #f7f8fa;
    --ml: #4338ca;
    --pos: #15803d;
    --neg: #b3261e;
    --warn-bg: #fdf2f2;
    --warn-br: #fecaca;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 48px 24px 96px;
    background: #fff;
    color: var(--ink);
    font: 15px/1.65 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Inter, Roboto, sans-serif;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  main { max-width: 880px; margin: 0 auto; }
  h1 { font-size: 30px; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 6px; }
  h2 { font-size: 20px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin: 52px 0 6px; }
  h3 { font-size: 15px; margin: 28px 0 8px; }
  p { margin: 12px 0; }
  .sub { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 28px; font-size: 15px; }
  .lead { font-size: 16.5px; }
  .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; margin-top: 4px; }
  hr { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--faint); margin: 44px 0 0; }

  .banner {
    background: var(--warn-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--warn-br);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    margin: 28px 0;
  }
  .banner h3 { margin: 0 0 6px; color: var(--neg); font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 0.02em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .banner p { margin: 6px 0; }
  .banner .verdict { font-size: 15px; }

  .card {
    border: 1px solid var(--faint);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    margin: 20px 0;
    background: #fff;
  }
  .card .k { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12.5px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
  .card .v { font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin-top: 2px; }
  .card .n { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; margin-top: 2px; }
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(170px, 1fr)); gap: 14px; margin: 20px 0; }

  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 16px 0; font-size: 14px; }
  th, td { text-align: right; padding: 9px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--faint); }
  th:first-child, td:first-child { text-align: left; }
  thead th { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; font-size: 12.5px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
  tbody tr:hover { background: var(--band); }
  td.num-pos { color: var(--pos); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  td.num-neg { color: var(--neg); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  td.naive { color: var(--muted); }
  td.ml { color: var(--ml); }
  .better { font-weight: 600; }

  figure { margin: 24px 0; }
  figure img { width: 100%; height: auto; border: 1px solid var(--faint); border-radius: 10px; }
  figcaption { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; margin-top: 8px; }

  code {
    font: 13px/1.5 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    background: var(--band); padding: 2px 5px; border-radius: 4px;
  }
  pre { background: var(--band); padding: 14px 16px; border-radius: 8px; overflow-x: auto; }
  pre code { background: none; padding: 0; }
  ul { padding-left: 22px; }
  li { margin: 5px 0; }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  .note { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--muted); border-left: 2px solid var(--faint); padding-left: 14px; }
  footer { margin-top: 64px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; border-top: 1px solid var(--faint); padding-top: 18px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>

<h1>Prediction Market Lab</h1>
<p class="sub">Research report — multi-vertical signal evaluation against a pre-committed gate</p>
<p class="meta">
  Experiment: <code>{{ experiment }}</code>
  {%- if experiment_date %} · {{ experiment_date }}{% endif %}
</p>

<div class="banner">
  <h3>Result</h3>
  <p class="verdict"><strong>The evaluation gate failed.</strong> The criterion was
  &ldquo;{{ gate.criterion }}&rdquo;, and the answer was no.</p>
  <p>{{ gate.rationale }}</p>
  {% if gate.best_vertical %}
  <p class="muted">Best vertical: {{ gate.best_vertical }}</p>
  {% endif %}
</div>

<p class="lead">This report documents a research pipeline built to answer one question:
does a machine-learned signal beat a trivial baseline on prediction-market contracts?
The pipeline produced a <strong>negative answer</strong>, and that answer is the
deliverable. The evaluation was pre-committed, the baseline was simple enough to
audit, and the conclusion was confirmed against live paper-trading data.</p>

<h2>1. The evaluation gate</h2>

<p>Before the experiment ran, the go/no-go criterion was written down and the model
was required to beat the naive baseline on at least one vertical. It beat it on none.</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Vertical</th>
      <th>Naive Sharpe</th><th>Naive hit</th><th>ML Sharpe</th><th>ML hit</th><th>ML accuracy</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for row in comparison %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ row.vertical }}</td>
      <td class="naive {% if row.naive_sharpe > row.ml_sharpe %}better{% endif %}">
        {{ "%.3f" | format(row.naive_sharpe) }}</td>
      <td class="naive">{{ "%.1f%%" | format(row.naive_hit * 100) }}</td>
      <td class="ml">{{ "%.3f" | format(row.ml_sharpe) }}</td>
      <td class="ml">{{ "%.1f%%" | format(row.ml_hit * 100) }}</td>
      <td class="ml">
        {%- if row.ml_accuracy is not none -%}
          {{ "%.3f" | format(row.ml_accuracy) }}
        {%- else -%}—{%- endif -%}
      </td>
    </tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<p class="note">The <code>{{ sharpest.vertical }}</code> row is the sharpest illustration. The model
reached {{ "%.0f%%" | format(sharpest.ml_accuracy * 100) }} classification accuracy
on its own test set while producing a Sharpe of
{{ "%.2f" | format(sharpest.ml_sharpe) }}. Accuracy against a synthetic
distribution is not edge.</p>

<figure>
  <img src="assets/sharpe-by-vertical.png" alt="Sharpe ratio by vertical, naive baseline versus ML model">
  <figcaption>Sharpe by vertical. The naive baseline (grey) beats the ML model (indigo) on every vertical.</figcaption>
</figure>

<figure>
  <img src="assets/hit-rate-by-vertical.png" alt="Hit rate by vertical, naive baseline versus ML model">
  <figcaption>Hit rate against the 50% break-even line for a binary contract.</figcaption>
</figure>

<h2>2. Backtest equity by vertical</h2>

<figure>
  <img src="assets/backtest-equity.png" alt="Backtest equity curve by vertical">
  <figcaption>Every vertical starts from the same bankroll. Weather and economics hold up;
  politics and sports give it back.</figcaption>
</figure>

<h2>3. Live paper run</h2>

<p>Backtests are not evidence. The bot was run against the live Kalshi API in paper
mode for 3.7 days with the risk engine and execution layer enabled.</p>

<div class="grid">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="k">Sharpe</div>
    <div class="v" style="color: var(--neg)">{{ "%.3f" | format(paper.sharpe) }}</div>
    <div class="n">{{ paper.n_trades }} trades filled</div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="k">Total PnL</div>
    <div class="v" style="color: var(--neg)">{{ money(paper.total_pnl_cents) }}</div>
    <div class="n">on {{ money(paper.final_bankroll_cents - paper.total_pnl_cents) }}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="k">Max drawdown</div>
    <div class="v">{{ "%.2f%%" | format(paper.max_drawdown_pct * 100) }}</div>
    <div class="n">risk engine enabled</div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="k">Hit rate</div>
    <div class="v">{{ "%.1f%%" | format(paper.hit_rate * 100) }}</div>
    <div class="n">below the 50% line</div>
  </div>
</div>

<figure>
  <img src="assets/paper-equity.png" alt="Live paper run equity curve">
  <figcaption>Bankroll over the live paper run, with per-trade PnL beneath.</figcaption>
</figure>

<h3>Fill log</h3>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Ticker</th><th>Vertical</th><th>Side</th><th>Entry</th><th>Outcome</th><th>PnL</th><th>Bankroll</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for row in paper_rows %}
    <tr>
      <td><code>{{ row.ticker }}</code></td>
      <td>{{ row.vertical }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.side }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.entry }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.outcome }}</td>
      <td class="{{ 'num-pos' if row.pnl_raw >= 0 else 'num-neg' }}">{{ row.pnl }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.bankroll }}</td>
    </tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<p class="note">{{ "{:,}".format(paper.n_signals_skipped) }} signals were skipped to
{{ paper.n_signals_fired }} fired. A strategy that has to reject 99.95% of its own
signals has been over-fitted to noise.</p>

<h2>4. What these numbers do and do not mean</h2>

<div class="banner">
  <h3>Read this before quoting any number above</h3>
  <p><strong>The backtests run against a synthetic simulator, not historical market
  data.</strong> The market generator builds deterministic, seeded markets whose
  true probability is derived from fundamentals stubs, and the backtester runs
  against that simulator rather than the exchange API.</p>
  <p>So the Sharpe figures measure <em>whether the model can fit the simulator</em>,
  not whether the strategy makes money. That is precisely why the model scores well
  on classification accuracy and badly on Sharpe. The live paper run is the only
  real-world measurement in this report, and it is small — 3.7 days, nine closed
  trades.</p>
</div>

<h3>What can be concluded</h3>
<ul>
  <li>The ML signal did not beat a trivial baseline on synthetic data, and the
      pre-committed gate was failed.</li>
  <li>The live paper run confirmed the direction, with a Sharpe of
      {{ "%.3f" | format(paper.sharpe) }}.</li>
  <li>The pipeline — simulator, backtester, risk engine, execution simulator, PnL
      ledger, paper runner, live telemetry — is sound enough that its verdict can
      be trusted.</li>
</ul>

<h3>What cannot be concluded</h3>
<ul>
  <li>That the strategy is worthless on real markets. The synthetic simulator and
      3.7 days of paper trading are not a fair test of a real edge.</li>
  <li>Anything precise about the Sharpe. Nine trades is a direction, not an estimate.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Reproduction</h2>

<p>The report is generated from the JSON in <code>research/data/</code>:</p>
<pre><code>python3 -m venv .venv &amp;&amp; .venv/bin/pip install matplotlib jinja2
.venv/bin/python -m research.build_report</code></pre>

<p>Backtest parameters used for this experiment:</p>
<ul>
  {%- for key, value in (params.backtest or {}).items() %}
  <li><code>{{ key }}</code>: <code>{{ value }}</code></li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>

<footer>
  Generated by <code>research/build_report.py</code>. Charts are rendered with
  matplotlib; the page is a static Jinja2 template with no client-side JavaScript.
</footer>

</main>
</body>
</html>
